{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a visible light photoredox-catalyzed decarboxylative alkylation of 3-aryl-oxetanes and azetidines. Using an iridium photocatalyst and cesium carbonate base, the authors generate tertiary benzylic radicals from carboxylic acid precursors, which then undergo Giese addition into various electron-deficient alkenes. The study highlights how ring strain in four-membered heterocycles increases radical reactivity and \u03c0-delocalization, favoring productive C-C bond formation over dimerization compared to unstrained benzylic systems.",
